  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "The best result so far is config_021 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, acc=0.725, 3.60 GPU hrs), which clearly establishes that scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, and transformer aggregation are the strongest components. The only untested variation on this exact architecture is the fusion strategy: config_031 swaps weighted fusion for concat. This is the most direct exploitation step—it isolates a single variable (fusion type) on the proven best backbone, so any accuracy change is cleanly attributable. If concat outperforms weighted, we get a new best; if not, we confirm weighted is optimal and can focus remaining budget on other axes (e.g., singleprofile or alternative encoders). Expected cost is similar to config_021 (~3.5–4 GPU hrs), making it a cheap, high-information experiment that tightens the search around the current best before spending the remaining 4 experiments on broader exploration."
}

